<a2ui>$/={terms_data:[{term:"Deductible",means:"A fixed amount you must pay before the insurer pays any admissible claim. In indemnity plans, it is a rupee. [3]",effect:"The insurer starts paying only after deductible is crossed."},{term:"Co-payment",means:"A percentage of the admissible claim that you must bear. It does not reduce the sum insured, but it reduces what the insurer pays for that claim.",effect:"You share the bill in a fixed ratio, such as 0% or 20%."},{term:"Waiting period",means:"A period after policy start during which certain claims are not payable. Standard policies generally have a30-day initial waiting period, and pre-existing-disease waiting periods are commonly cappedat366 months in newer IRDA-regulated-products [7]",effect:"Claims during the waiting period may be fully rejected."},{term:"Room-rent limit",means:"A cap on the hospital room charge covered by the policy, often linked to a percentage of the sum insured. [2]",effect:"If you choose alier room, some policies reduce payment for other hospital charges in the same proportion."},{term:"Exclusions",means:"Treatments or situations the policy does not cover at all, such as pre-existing disease during the waiting period, many non-medical items, cosmetic, and other exclusions. [3][2][0]",effect:"The insurer pays nothing for excluded items or events."}]}
